\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces How much each attribution method dilutes a repeated frame, under controlled repetition (E1). The change in the score of one copy of the target divided by the model's own change, $r_\phi / r_I$, per target, then the median over targets; 1 means that the score follows the model. Largest number of copies tested (four times the reference on R3D-50 and R3D-18, nine times on MC3-18 and V-JEPA2, two times on TRN); exact copies. Leave-one-out uses deletion except on TRN (grey), where only freezing is possible and part of the result is fixed by the operator (Section~\ref {sec:removal}).}}{13}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bias-map}{{1}{13}{How much each attribution method dilutes a repeated frame, under controlled repetition (E1). The change in the score of one copy of the target divided by the model's own change, $r_\phi / r_I$, per target, then the median over targets; 1 means that the score follows the model. Largest number of copies tested (four times the reference on R3D-50 and R3D-18, nine times on MC3-18 and V-JEPA2, two times on TRN); exact copies. Leave-one-out uses deletion except on TRN (grey), where only freezing is possible and part of the result is fixed by the operator (Section~\ref {sec:removal})}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Leave-one-out under controlled repetition, at the largest number of copies tested. ``Copies'' is the number of copies of the target relative to the reference clip. $r_I$ is the model's own change in dependence on the target. Score per copy: the mean leave-one-out score of one copy of the target, relative to the reference clip, for the target clip and for the control clip. $\beta $: dilution slope with 95\% bootstrap interval ($\beta = -1$ is an even split among the copies). Medians over targets. Exact copies. Freezing rows for TRN, and for R3D-50 and R3D-18 for comparison, are marked $^\dagger $: their scores are partly fixed by the operator.}}{13}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e1-loo}{{2}{13}{Leave-one-out under controlled repetition, at the largest number of copies tested. ``Copies'' is the number of copies of the target relative to the reference clip. $r_I$ is the model's own change in dependence on the target. Score per copy: the mean leave-one-out score of one copy of the target, relative to the reference clip, for the target clip and for the control clip. $\beta $: dilution slope with 95\% bootstrap interval ($\beta = -1$ is an even split among the copies). Medians over targets. Exact copies. Freezing rows for TRN, and for R3D-50 and R3D-18 for comparison, are marked $^\dagger $: their scores are partly fixed by the operator}{table.2}{}}
